<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>
<span id="S3.T1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effectiveness Results.</span>
The best results are marked in <span id="S3.T1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>.
All the explicit planning methods (
<span id="S3.T1.10" class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-toggle-on" aria-hidden="true">
</span>) use explicit knowledge to guide executors.

<span id="S3.T1.11" class="ltx_inline-block fas fa-toggle-off" aria-hidden="true">
</span> represents prompt engineering methods and implicit planning methods without global foresight.
<span id="S3.T1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">Red</span> shows the changes of EAGLET relative to the the baselines without global plans.
Executor agents w/ training baselines are implemented on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al. (2025)</a></cite>.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we conduct experiments and analyses to show the effectiveness of EAGLET.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Experiment Settings</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Benchmarks.</span>
We conducted experiments on ScienceWorld <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>, ALFWorld <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shridhar et al., 2021</a>)</cite>, and WebShop <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.
ScienceWorld presents a challenging benchmark for complete scientific experiments in a highly interactive environment.
ALFWorld contains household tasks that require agents to explore rooms and accomplish objectives.
WebShop is a web-based interactive environment designed to test agents in realistic online shopping scenarios.
Both ALFWorld and ScienceWorld include seen and unseen scenarios to assess in-distribution and out-of-distribution generalization of the agents separately.
In contrast, WebShop only contains seen scenarios for testing.
More details are shown in Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Dataset Details ‣ A Goal Without a Plan Is Just a Wish: Efficient and Effective Global Planner Training for Long-Horizon Agent Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span>
We fully compare the proposed method with a series of baselines, including:
(1) <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Closed-source LLMs</span>: We test four state-of-the-art models, namely GPT-4.1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2023</a>)</cite>, GPT-5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI, 2025</a>)</cite>, DeepSeek-V3.1-Non-Think <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, and DeepSeek-V3.1-Think, which represent advanced capabilities in reasoning and understanding.
(2) <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implicit planning methods</span>: These works enhance agent planning capabilities via parameter updates.
AgentTuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng et al., 2024</a>)</cite> uses SFT on collected trajectories to improve the task-solving capabilities.
ETO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song et al., 2024b</a>)</cite> further teaches executor agents to learn from failed trajectories using an exploration-based trajectory optimization method.
GiGPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng et al., 2025</a>)</cite> proposes a novel outcome-based RL algorithm that achieves fine-grained reward assignment for training the executor agent.
(3) <span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Explicit planning methods</span>: These methods try to use explicit knowledge to guide executor agents.
WKM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qiao et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and KnowAgent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> collect the prior knowledge and incorporate external action knowledge into the executor agent training.
MPO <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al., 2025</a>)</cite> trains a planner model to provide the global guidance via applying SFT on human-modified data and DPO training.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Metrics and Evaluation.</span>
ScienceWorld and WebShop provide dense final rewards ranging from 0 to 1 to measure the completion level of the task, whereas ALFWorld offers only binary rewards indicating whether the agent has completed the task.
For all the datasets, we apply <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">average reward</span> as the metric, which calculates the mean reward across all task instances.
We also report the success rate in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Implementation and Evaluation Details ‣ A Goal Without a Plan Is Just a Wish: Efficient and Effective Global Planner Training for Long-Horizon Agent Tasks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.
For evaluation, we apply ReAct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2023</a>)</cite> prompting with a one-shot in-context example following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiong et al. (2025)</a></cite> to leverage these models’ abilities.
However, GiGPO is an exception: we use the prompt from the original paper <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Feng et al., 2025</a>)</cite> as the GiGPO method does not employ ReAct-style prompts during RL training.</p>
</div>
